# 2. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a centralized platform that allows users to manage physical Android SIM cards remotely through a web browser.

Each Android phone acts as an SMS Gateway device.

The Android application receives SMS commands from the backend and uses the phone's physical SIM card to send messages.

Incoming SMS messages are forwarded from the Android application to the backend.

The website is the main control panel through which users manage all SMS operations.

Users must be able to:

- Connect Android phones using QR codes.
- View connected devices.
- Monitor device connectivity.
- Receive incoming SMS messages in real time.
- Send individual SMS messages.
- Send bulk SMS messages.
- View sent message history.
- View delivery reports where supported.
- Configure AI Auto Reply.
- Configure automation rules.
- Manage contacts and recipient groups.
- Monitor sending queues.
- View usage statistics.
- Manage device settings.
- Disconnect devices.
- Monitor errors and failed messages.

The platform should support multiple users and multiple Android devices per account.

Every user's data must be isolated.

