# 10. SHARED WEBSOCKET EVENT CONTRACT

All events must use this JSON envelope:

{
  "event": "EVENT_NAME",
  "event_id": "unique-event-id",
  "device_id": "device-uuid",
  "timestamp": "2026-11-08T12:00:00Z",
  "payload": {}
}

## Events sent by backend to Android

### SMS_SEND_COMMAND

{
  "event": "SMS_SEND_COMMAND",
  "event_id": "event-uuid",
  "device_id": "device-uuid",
  "timestamp": "ISO-8601",
  "payload": {
    "command_id": "command-uuid",
    "message_id": "message-uuid",
    "recipient": "+2557XXXXXXXX",
    "message_body": "Your message here.",
    "subscription_id": 1,
    "idempotency_key": "unique-key"
  }
}

### DEVICE_CONFIG_UPDATE

Used to update permitted device configuration.

### PING

Used for connection health checks.

### DEVICE_DISCONNECT

Used to revoke or terminate an authorized device connection.

### COMMAND_CANCEL

Used to cancel commands that have not yet been executed.

## Events received from Android

- DEVICE_CONNECTED
- DEVICE_HEARTBEAT
- DEVICE_DISCONNECTED
- SMS_RECEIVED
- SMS_SENT
- SMS_DELIVERED
- SMS_FAILED
- COMMAND_ACKNOWLEDGED
- DEVICE_STATUS

Validate all incoming event structures.

Never trust device-supplied user IDs.

Resolve ownership from the authenticated device record.

