# 19. REAL-TIME WEBSITE COMMUNICATION

The website must receive updates without refreshing the page.

Use authenticated WebSocket connections.

Website connection:

wss://api.yourdomain.com/user/connect

Authenticate the website user securely.

The backend must subscribe each connection to the correct user's events.

Required website events:

- DEVICE_CONNECTED
- DEVICE_DISCONNECTED
- DEVICE_STATUS
- SMS_RECEIVED
- SMS_QUEUED
- SMS_SENT
- SMS_DELIVERED
- SMS_FAILED
- CAMPAIGN_PROGRESS
- CAMPAIGN_COMPLETED
- AI_REPLY_GENERATED
- AI_REPLY_FAILED

Use the following event envelope:

{
  "event": "SMS_RECEIVED",
  "event_id": "event-uuid",
  "timestamp": "ISO-8601",
  "payload": {}
}

Ensure that events are delivered only to the appropriate account.

Do not broadcast private SMS data to all connected users.

Implement reconnection and state resynchronization.

WebSocket events are notifications, not the source of truth. The website must be able to reload current state from REST APIs after reconnecting.

